            <div xml:id="d101">

                <pb facs="0099" n="91" sameAs="frus:frus1937v04/pg91"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94 Conference/62</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Department of State to
                        the British Embassy</hi></head>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Memorandum of Conversation With
                        Mr. Mallet, British Chargé d’Affaires, October</hi> 19, 1937</p>
                <p>In discussing with Mr. Mallet the <hi rendition="#italic">aide-mémoire</hi> of
                    October 18th, which the British Chargé d’Affaires had been good enough to bring
                    to the attention of the Government of the United States concerning a further
                    meeting of the Advisory Committee, Mr. Wilson stated that, since the Government
                    of the United States was not a member of the League of Nations, it had refrained
                    scrupulously at any time from endeavoring to influence League bodies in such
                    action as they might choose to adopt. It is to be remembered that the American
                    representative sitting on the Advisory Committee does so without the right to
                    vote.</p>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1937-10-19">October 19,
                            1937</date>.</dateline>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
